   {
    "text": "**The Ball of Tennis, in Medieval Style**\n\nIn ancient courts, where knights and lords did play,  \nA ball of leather, soft and bright, was laid.  \nWith feathers, spun from threads of fine and rare,  \nIt danced with grace, and sparks did arise.  \n\nThe court was round, and the players stood,  \nWith sticks of oak, and gloves of wool, they'd go.  \nThe ball, though small, was mighty in its flight,  \nA test of skill, and strength, and might.  \n\nIt was of leather, thick and strong,  \nWith feathers, like the wings of a great bird,  \nIt flew with speed, and with a soft, light sound,  \nA ball of tennis, in medieval mood.  \n\nP.P.S. — Though modern rules differ, the ball remains,  \nA symbol of the game, both old and new.",
